"status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-07","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Please note this meeting has moved from 22 July","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Cancelled; Reserve date for call in - NOT REQUIRED","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; At the rising of the preceding General Purposes Committee, no earlier than 7 pm","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Council has committed \u00a320m to Levelling Up Fund capital projects currently in progress.","lead":"Large capital commitments carry delivery and financial risk. A lender assesses capital strategy, project delivery track record, and funding sources.","iso":"2026-07-14","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 (1) MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134657/134657.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Cyber incident is identified as one of the three highest-scoring risks on the Strategic Risk Register.","lead":"Cyber incidents can result in direct financial loss, service disruption, or compliance breaches. Identification as highest risk suggests material vulnerability exposure.","iso":"2026-07-14","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 (1) MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134657/134657.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Housing function underwent external governance review by the Housing Regulatory Inspector with formal action plan oversight.","lead":"Housing is typically a material financial function for councils. External governance review signals control weaknesses or service problems that could affect financial outcomes or compliance.","iso":"2026-07-14","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 (1) MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134657/134657.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 (1) MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134657/134657.pdf","headline":"Council has committed \u00a320m to Levelling Up Fund capital projects currently in progress.","detail":"Large capital enhancement projects are underway, described as delivering over \u00a320m in public realm and historic environment improvements. These projects are intended to leave a legacy following the Local Government Reorganisation.","category":"capital","matters":"Large capital commitments carry delivery and financial risk. A lender assesses capital strategy, project delivery track record, and funding sources.","figures":"\u00a320m total Levelling Up Fund projects","quote":"Several large projects are in progress, including the Levelling Up Fund projects, delivering over \u00a320m of enhancements to the public realm and historic elements of Canterbury that will leave a legacy post-reorganisation.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 (1) MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134657/134657.pdf","headline":"Cyber incident is identified as one of the three highest-scoring risks on the Strategic Risk Register.","detail":"Cyber resilience is explicitly noted as a priority focus area. Cyber incident features alongside LGR and external relationships as top-tier risks, indicating material concern about digital security and potential operational/financial impact.","category":"governance","matters":"Cyber incidents can result in direct financial loss, service disruption, or compliance breaches. Identification as highest risk suggests material vulnerability exposure.","figures":"Risk score range: 20 down to 9; cyber listed among highest scoring risks","quote":"The highest risk scores were concerned with: \u2022 Local Government Reorganisation \u2022 Relationships with Trusts and other outside bodies \u2022 Cyber incident","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 (1) MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134657/134657.pdf","headline":"Housing function underwent external governance review by the Housing Regulatory Inspector with formal action plan oversight.","detail":"The council has formally engaged with an external regulatory inspector on its housing function and is delivering a corrective action plan overseen by a dedicated Cabinet Committee. This indicates identified governance or service delivery issues in housing that require structured remediation.","category":"governance","matters":"Housing is typically a material financial function for councils. External governance review signals control weaknesses or service problems that could affect financial outcomes or compliance.","figures":"Not specified in this document","quote":"The housing function was recently reviewed by the Housing Regulatory Inspector. Delivery of the action plan arising from the review is being overseen by a Cabinet Committee.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"2025-26 TM outturn report draft (2)_Oksana Ivanova MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134648/134648.pdf","headline":"Council breached treasury investment limit on unsecured funds, reaching \u00a37.18m against \u00a35m policy ceiling","detail":"During 2025-26, unsecured building society investments reached \u00a37.18m, exceeding the council's \u00a35m policy limit. The council states the breach lasted 'one night only' due to timing of fund arrivals, and was corrected the next day. However, the council frames the \u00a35m limit as guidance rather than binding policy, treating the exceedance as a minor administrative lapse rather than a control failure.","category":"governance","matters":"A treasury control allowing deviation from stated investment limits\u2014even if brief\u2014suggests the operational framework does not reliably enforce its own risk thresholds; this is relevant to assessing whether the council's treasury function can be relied upon","figures":"Maximum during year \u00a37.18m; limit \u00a35m; difference \u00a32.18m","quote":"The balance went above this level for one night only, because funds arrived in the account after the cut off time for placing them into more secure investments fund. The \u00a37m was moved out the very next day into higher security deposit funds, so the position was quickly adjusted.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-14","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"2025-26 TM outturn report draft (2)_Oksana Ivanova MT","paper_url":"https://democracy.canterbury.gov.uk/documents/s134648/134648.pdf","headline":"Whitefriars retail investment income remains below pre-pandemic levels, threatened by structural retail sector decline","detail":"Canterbury holds a strategic \u00a379.2m investment in the Whitefriars Development Unit Trust. The investment generated \u00a35.2m income in 2025-26, but this remains materially below pre-pandemic levels. The council attributes this to documented structural headwinds in retail: declining high street rents, online competition, and economic uncertainty affecting rent reviews. While low vacancy rates are maintained, income sustainability from this material asset concentration remains constrained.","category":"income","matters":"A \u00a379.2m retail asset in structural decline is a significant income risk; underperformance relative to historical norms suggests the valuation and future income projections may not be resilient to further sector deterioration","figures":"\u00a379.2 million investment; \u00a35.2 million income 2025-26; income below pre-pandemic levels","quote":"This strategic non-treasury investment generated \u00a35.2 million of income in 2025-26. Income levels remain below those achieved prior to the pandemic, reflecting ongoing pressures within the retail sector. Nationally, high street retail rents have declined due to changing consumer behaviour, increased online competition, and continued economic uncertainty.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-14"},"name":"Canterbury","findings_total":55,"news_drafts_total":3}}